"Stu-art'h, called Stuart by Alden Thorn, is an Artonan boy and the son of the Primary."
"He has golden metal rings around his irises and uncommon body modifications."
"He is short and skinny but heavy, because his bones are enhanced."
"He is older than Alden, though he looks younger."
"He wants to become a Knight of the Mother Planet and serve the Triplanets."
"At LeafSong an illicitly summoned mishnen bit off his foot, which surgeons later reattached."
"Alden preserved Stuart with his skill until the foot could be reattached."
"The cover story for his injury is a duel with Jel-nor."
"He called his injury a trial of suffering and apologized in English for tarnishing their honor."
"After the injury he wore a white gel boot and was guarded by five Artonans in green."
"His aunt is Knight Alis-art'h, and his sister Sina-art'h was a knight."
"He is in the youngest class of knight students and is quite sensitive."
"He noticed Alden's unusual authority and told his father."
"He has bright rust-colored irises and brown hair, half shaved and half French-braided."
"At university he ranks in the top seven percent but is awkward and has no friends there."
"He mourned Alden by raising a bright red pet ryeh-b't named Alden."
"His foot keeps nerve damage until he finishes contemplating his errors, an ancient practice."
"Alden once slapped his nose and called him a prick during the mishnen incident."
"He invited Alden back to the Art'h Residence as a guest for cultural studies."
"He attends LeafSong early to make a point about himself, and lives mostly on Artona III."
"Since Alden came back alive, he calls his pet ryeh-b't Other Alden."
"He calls Alden on his weekends, about every thirteen Earth days."
"He told Alden: you never say anything that makes me hate you."
"In November, after more than eight months, his foot was finally healed."
"His auriad is very pale purple; he casts elegantly and makes spell rings."
"He cannot call Avowed himself, so Evul-art'h places his calls."
"He sent Alden a wizard learning cushion by Craftswoman Enyl-tirg through the Artonan embassy."
"He is the Primary's youngest child and may not talk to Avowed without supervision."
"He is about to make an irrevocable life choice."
"During the flood he told Joe volunteers were being sworn in to aid Earth at the Grand Senate."
"His family held a negotiation after he admitted Alden never signed Privacy of the House."
"He then invited Alden to the Rapport, the art'h home, and Alden accepted."
"His mother was the knight Iella-inwer; he was born off the Triplanets."
"He grew up inside his mother's mind trap until his father freed him."
"A vision of his mother lingers with him, and he suffers episodes."
"He bears the mourning name Sina for his dead sister, whose votary he had meant to be."
"He announced he would be a knight half a year before meeting Alden, horrifying his family."
"His chosen knight skill is The Maker of Narrow Ways, which forces tunnels through things."
"Many expect him to die of his first binding, and his family asked him to delay it."
"He recommended Joe be sent to Anesidora after the flood."
"He collects husenots, rock-like pets that have their own room."
"Only Alden calls him Stuart; everyone else calls him Stu."
"For a while he serves as votary to Emban-art'h."
"He arranged for the mind healer Yenu-pezth to meet Alden."
"His father once took him to another healer against Yenu-pezth's advice."
"He overheard his parents discussing using Alden to turn him from knighthood, and was hurt."
"As a Declared, one who has chosen knighthood before first affixation, he is shunned at school."
"He sees Maker of Narrow Ways as rooted in connection, even though it severs."
"He told Alden the truth about how Joe left his Thegund scientists."
"His older brother Jozz is a knight whose portrait hangs in Rapport School's top library."
"He hates that painting, since Jozz looks lonely, waiting for Sina who will never come."
"As Emban's votary at her Here-to-There, he learned a shade spell after watching it once."
"He introduced Alden as his future lifelong friend and plans to swear friendship oaths to him."
"He says his choosing season is over and he will move toward his first binding regardless."
"His authority is much stronger than Alden's, closer to Lute's level."
"He bolstered Alden's skill by touching his being, an approach Avowed cannot refuse."
"He means to use his skill to make a universe with fewer places like Thegund."
"His formal name is Sina Stu-art'h, a votary wizard of the First Rapport."
"He took Olget's wand-breaking to executioner Vill-ma and refused to unsay his accusation."
"His first binding is delayed half a year, to be held at home with two other Rapports' Declared."
"He promised Alden a place in his first binding ceremony."
"His mind trap is almost gone; he says the mind trap is how his mother loved him."
"His LeafSong roommate is Bayab-oth."
"He wrote a friendship study journal meant for only two people, him and Alden."
"He suspects Kon's skill was made for work on the Sdyelis Branch, an unfinished oasis ship."
"At Welcome End he passed his oath ceremony at DawnStep, and wears his Declared mark on his coat."
"He paid for Alden's learning cushion by clearing expired ingredients from village cabinets."
"His favorite food is bread dipped in ceremonial wevvi, a comfort learned from his father."
"As a child he lived with his mother by a river of patient creatures, which he embroiders."
"Rel says he lacks the kind of confidence the family wants him to have."
"He secretly researches protection-concept skills to complement Alden's skill."
"He studies skill theory so Alden never again affixes a skill he doesn't understand."
"He will train at Goldbush as a knight."
"He has a video, obtained by his father, of Alden holding him during his leg restoration."
"On his father's advice he may secretly take his first binding well before Welcome End."
"He calls Calassa Calassa Mom; of his father's spouses he is closest to Olorn and Veln."
"At LeafSong he shares a canopy house with Bayab-oth and Eeaner-ket, and rescues klerms."
"After the mishnen debacle he swore off parties with sex or mood-altering experiences."
"Asay-tor told him knighthood is too dangerous for him; Stu called him a prick and shoved him."
"When Alden revealed he is a wizard, Stu said yes to everything Alden is and wants from him."
"His first spell, taught by his mother, was a finger chime."
"He decided not to tell his parents about Alden until after he becomes a knight."
"He begins to suspect Ro-den is behind Alden's strange secrecy about his skill."
"He spoke Rityan as a child, before learning modern Artonan."
"Spying through his eye rings, he deduced Ro-den's contract hides Alden's skill."
"He told Ro-den: I think you might be evil, I'm going to find out, and then I'll fix it."
"He built an art'h-wood greeting house at the House of Healing and trapped Ro-den with its table."
"He offered Ro-den Renjen-art'h's demon hide chest, and Ro-den freed Alden from the contract."
"He is scared of his first binding and refuses to become anyone's votary."
"As a child he was tutored a year in poetry performance to build his confidence."
"He gave Ro-den the art'h hide without his family's permission or knowledge."
